WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:07.700
CompTIA Network Plus, domain 1, Networking concepts, which is 23 percent of the exam.

00:00:07.700 --> 00:00:10.315
This lesson covers objective 1 point 8.

00:00:10.315 --> 00:00:14.406
Summarize evolving use cases for modern network environments.

00:00:14.406 --> 00:00:20.240
Today's concept: the three planes of a network device, and which one builds the tables.

00:00:22.570 --> 00:00:25.221
Every router and switch does three jobs.

00:00:25.221 --> 00:00:27.010
Each job is called a plane.

00:00:27.330 --> 00:00:32.390
The management plane is how you configure the device, for example over SSH or SNMP.

00:00:32.730 --> 00:00:34.351
The control plane is the brain.

00:00:34.351 --> 00:00:37.070
It builds the routing table and the switching table.

00:00:37.400 --> 00:00:38.952
The data plane does the work.

00:00:38.952 --> 00:00:41.894
For every packet it looks up the table and forwards it.

00:00:41.894 --> 00:00:43.660
It never builds the table itself.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:48.546
A common mistake is to say management plane, because you configure things there.

00:00:48.546 --> 00:00:50.990
But configuring is not building the tables.

00:00:53.330 --> 00:00:57.940
In software-defined networking, the control plane moves into one central controller.

00:00:58.270 --> 00:01:01.527
The controller pushes forwarding rules down to the switches.

00:01:01.527 --> 00:01:03.590
The switches keep only the data plane.

00:01:05.930 --> 00:01:09.354
On the exam, ask who builds the routing and switching tables.

00:01:09.354 --> 00:01:10.814
That is the control plane.

00:01:10.814 --> 00:01:15.698
The data plane only forwards, and the management plane is how you configure the device.

00:01:15.698 --> 00:01:17.550
That's objective one point eight.
